Z||000000||fiero56||05-10-2001||10:18 PM||||I've got an '86SE with the grey two-tone dash. Dark on top, light on bottom. I <B>hate</B> the lighter grey on the dash and want to replaint the entire dash, the color of the original dark grey, so that it will match intrument shrouds, etc. <P>Aynbody know what paint matches the darker grey shade as closely as possible? I doubt I would need any paint with flex agents, as the dash doesn't see much abuse, plus it isn't able to flex much. Any ideas what to use?||||reg||5
Z||000001||DXR_DAD||05-10-2001||10:38 PM||||I would head to the local upholstery shop and get all the info I need, See if they can match the color, and sell you what you need.<P><BR>DXR_DAD||||reg||1
Z||000002||FieroLisa||05-10-2001||10:58 PM||||I think PPG has a book with all the paint colors, look under Pontiac 1986 and there will be your color!<P>I agree you won't need a flex agent for the dash, but if you plan on doing that center console or armrest thingies you'll definitely need it. Oh and Prep Well!! It'll save you a ton of time in the long run!<P>||||reg||1
Z||000003||sjp777||05-11-2001||12:41 AM||||I'm not sure about paint for the vinyl, but if you want to paint the plastic trim pieces over and under the doors and the rear pillars where the speaker grills are, Duplicolor graphite is almost a perfect match with the dark gray on the upper dash<P>------------------<BR> <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fiero88gt1/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/fiero88gt1/</A>||||reg||1
Z||000004||maryjane||05-11-2001||12:55 AM||||A sad tale to tell. My better half decided she didn't like the grey in her 84 interior, so she painted it black. Not just the dash & console, ALL OF IT! Door panels,headliner,floor carpets,everything. Couldn't believe it. took forever to get overspray off the instrument cluster/windows.<BR>First thing happens,thinner in the paint made the headliner fall. Now she has to re-touch every month on arm rests and door ledge. Looks like ka-ka now(hope she doesn't read this) <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000005||Songman||05-11-2001||01:18 AM||||The same thing has been done to the T-top I just bought.... Perfectly good tan interior completely spray painted black! Looks like *@#%!<P>It is your car, but from my experience I would never paint a car interior.. Good luck to you if you try it...<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
Z||000006||fiero56||05-11-2001||01:23 AM||||You guys do know that most all interior trim pieces were painted at the factory, right?||||reg||1
Z||000007||mrfiero||05-11-2001||01:41 AM||||All hard plastic trim was molded the proper color, but most of the soft vinyl was paint to match.  I know the dash and the radio pod were painted to match.  <P>You will have no problem painting the dash.  I think a lot of people are misunderstanding the term "paint".  They make a good vinyl/plastic paint that works very well (it's not "real" paint).  SEM makes a very good quality vinyl paint and you can get the proper color gray already in the spray can from most paint stores and even K-Mart.<P>I have had some '88 tan (dark sienna, light sienna, med. beechwood) custom mixed for me at a local paint shop and put into spray cans.....it's an exact match and has held up great.<P>Prep is very important......you must remove all of the waxes, dirt, etc left over from all of those Armor-All applications otherwise the new "paint" won't stick.  SEM also sells a plastic and vinyl prep in a spray can......clean the dash with soap and water then use the prep spray.  Spray the vinyl paint in several thin coats and no one will be able to tell it wasn't original.<P>Good luck.  ||||reg||1
Z||000008||Songman||05-11-2001||01:43 AM||||Wish someone had done all this to mine... it looks awful... and spray painted carpet! Yuck! Good thing I was planning to do a custom interior anyway..<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
Z||000009||Carrolles||05-12-2001||12:39 AM||||I believe the SEM Graphite Grey is a pretty close match.  I used it on the speaker grills (per Mr. Mike's suggestion) and it looks great||||reg||1
